   "updated": 1735689600000,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "- Four tokens do the work: T1 gets a person into Foundry, T2 carries the person through the gateway and the MCP server, T3 is the server's own identity, and T4 reaches data as that\n  person.\n- Every token names its audience. T2 for one server fails at the others, and T4 works only at the one data service it was issued for.\n- The static secrets (C3, C5, C6) are long-lived, shared and carry no user. The four data-backed MCP servers hold none of them: they use managed identities.",
   "fontSize": 18,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "originalText": "- Four tokens do the work: T1 gets a person into Foundry, T2 carries the person through the gateway and the MCP server, T3 is the server's own identity, and T4 reaches data as that\n  person.\n- Every token names its audience. T2 for one server fails at the others, and T4 works only at the one data service it was issued for.\n- The static secrets (C3, C5, C6) are long-lived, shared and carry no user. The four data-backed MCP servers hold none of them: they use managed identities.",
   "autoResize": true,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
